@startuml
left to right direction

' Defining our actors and their structural relationship
actor "Visitor" as visitor
actor "Logged-In Customer" as customer

' Inheritance: A Logged-In Customer can do everything a Visitor can do
customer -up-|> visitor

rectangle "Bank Application System" {
    ' Open features
    usecase "Create New Account" as UC_Register
    usecase "Select Account Type" as UC_Type
    usecase "Authenticate via PIN (Login)" as UC_Login

    ' Protected features (Inside the secure session)
    usecase "Deposit Funds" as UC_Deposit
    usecase "Withdraw Funds" as UC_Withdraw
    usecase "Check Balance" as UC_Balance
    usecase "View Transaction History" as UC_Statement
    usecase "Apply Interest" as UC_Interest
}

' What the basic visitor can do
visitor --> UC_Register
visitor --> UC_Login

' Account creation strictly includes picking a type
UC_Register ..> UC_Type : <<include>>

' What the authenticated customer can do
customer --> UC_Deposit
customer --> UC_Withdraw
customer --> UC_Balance
customer --> UC_Statement
customer --> UC_Interest

note right of UC_Interest
  Accessible only if
  account is SavingsAccount
end note

@enduml